<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aceh War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1873">1873</a>–<a href="/years/1904">1904</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> War was the long conflict between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> and the Aceh Sultanate in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, begun by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> invasion in 1873. The Dutch took the capital but faced decades of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> resistance led by Islamic scholars and chiefs. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-daud-syah">Muhammad Daud Syah</a> surrendered in 1903, though fighting went on for years, and the war completed Dutch control of the outer islands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aceh-war.jpg" alt="Aceh War" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Geschilderd naar Jules Garnier (Collectie Koninklijk Huisarchief in bruikleen aan museum Bronbeek) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samalanga_1878.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
